<%!-- Framed as an app window so it reads as a thing that happened rather than
      a diagram of one. Still markup: selectable, theme-aware, and the line in
      the first bubble is the same string as the paste block below it. --%>
<div class="chat-app">
  <div class="chat-bar">
    <span class="lights" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
    <span class="chat-title">Your assistant</span>
  </div>

  <%!-- `role="img"` sits on the transcript rather than the whole window. It has
        to: the role makes everything inside it presentational, and the composer
        below is now a real link. Labelling the window would have hidden that
        link from every screen reader.

        `tabindex` because the transcript scrolls, and a region that scrolls has
        to be reachable without a mouse. --%>
  <div class="chat" tabindex="0" role="img" aria-label="A conversation with an assistant: the visitor pastes the setup line, the assistant reads llms.txt, runs two calls, and returns Prospects.csv with twenty verified work emails.">
    <div class="turn you">
      <span class="avatar" aria-hidden="true">You</span>
      <div class="bubble" data-signed="out">
        Read <%= @base_url %>/llms.txt and use the CSuiteFinder API and store my
        token <code>csf_live_...</code> to be used. Then run /demo
      </div>
      <div class="bubble" data-signed="in" hidden>
        Read <%= @base_url %>/llms.txt and use the CSuiteFinder API and store my
        token <code data-key>CSF_KEY_HERE</code> to be used. Then run /demo
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="turn bot">
      <span class="avatar bot" aria-hidden="true">✦</span>
      <div class="bubble">
        <p class="lead">
          Read <code>llms.txt</code> — 18 endpoints, prices included. Token stored.
          Running <code>/demo</code>.
        </p>

        <div class="runs">
          <div class="run">
            <span class="tick" aria-hidden="true">✓</span>
            <span class="verb get">GET</span>
            <code>/email/company/people</code>
            <span class="args">domain=stripe.com · executive · limit 20</span>
            <span class="cost" data-aud="sales">included</span>
            <span class="cost" data-aud="developer" hidden>$0.05</span>
          </div>
          <div class="run">
            <span class="tick" aria-hidden="true">✓</span>
            <span class="verb post">POST</span>
            <code>/email/deliverable</code>
            <span class="args">× 20</span>
            <span class="cost">included</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="tally">
          <span class="pill ok">18 deliverable</span>
          <span class="pill bad">2 undeliverable</span>
          <span class="tally-note" data-aud="sales">out of this month's credit</span>
          <span class="tally-note" data-aud="developer" hidden>$0.05 spent</span>
        </div>

        <p class="settle">
          The two that would have bounced were caught before you sent to them.
        </p>

        <div class="file">
          <span class="file-icon" aria-hidden="true">CSV</span>
          <div class="file-meta">
            <strong>Prospects.csv</strong>
            <span>20 rows · name, title, email, deliverable</span>
          </div>
          <span class="file-done">Ready</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <%!-- The whole composer is the link, not just the arrow. Someone who wants to
        reply to this conversation clicks where they would type, and a box that
        looks like an input and does nothing when clicked is worse than no box.
        One anchor rather than two so there is a single focus stop and a single
        target, however far right the pointer lands. --%>
  <a class="composer" href="<%= CsuiteFinderWeb.Layout.sales_href() %>"
     aria-label="Email sales about CSuiteFinder"
     data-cta="chat_composer">
    <span class="composer-field">Ask for the next twenty<span class="dots" aria-hidden="true"><i>.</i><i>.</i><i>.</i></span></span>
    <span class="composer-send" aria-hidden="true">↑</span>
  </a>
</div>
